# Try the auth API by hand. VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client),
# start the server (`dotnet run` in server/), then click "Send Request" above each block.
# Cookies are remembered between requests, like a browser.
# Signup, login and recover each need a solved captcha, and each one works once: before every one of those
# requests, run `bash server/solve-altcha.sh` and paste its output over @altcha below.

@base = http://localhost:5137/api/auth
@username = alice
@password = my-long-passphrase
@altcha = paste-a-fresh-one-here

### A captcha challenge, as the widget fetches it (solve-altcha.sh does this and solves it for you)
GET {{base}}/challenge

### Who am I? (401 until you sign up or log in)
GET {{base}}/me

### Sign up: the response shows your recovery code ONCE
# @name signup
POST {{base}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}", "altcha": "{{altcha}}" }

### Log out
POST {{base}}/logout

### Log in
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}", "altcha": "{{altcha}}" }

### Forgot password: reset with the recovery code (gives you a NEW code; the old one stops working)
# Paste your code over the {{...}} below if you signed up in an earlier session.
POST {{base}}/recover
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "recoveryCode": "{{signup.response.body.$.recoveryCode}}", "newPassword": "another-long-passphrase", "altcha": "{{altcha}}" }

### Things that should fail: a common password
POST {{base}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "bob", "password": "password123", "altcha": "{{altcha}}" }
